You got this!

510
00:18:44,262 --> 00:18:47,232
(Preparing something)

511
00:18:48,402 --> 00:18:50,072
(Gently)

512
00:18:50,432 --> 00:18:52,071
- What's that? - What is that?

513
00:18:52,072 --> 00:18:53,171
What on earth is that?

514
00:18:53,172 --> 00:18:55,072
I must prevent my facial skin from sagging.

515
00:18:55,272 --> 00:18:56,411
My skin will sag.

516
00:18:56,412 --> 00:18:57,711
That's painful on the ears.

517
00:18:57,712 --> 00:18:59,071
(He finishes putting on the jawline mask.)

518
00:18:59,072 --> 00:19:00,312
Let's go.

519
00:19:01,612 --> 00:19:02,752
Start the GPS.

520
00:19:03,612 --> 00:19:06,782
Three, two, one. Go.

521
00:19:07,582 --> 00:19:08,942
(Starting today, I'm Moorathoner.)

522
00:19:09,922 --> 00:19:11,622
Let's take it slow.

523
00:19:12,292 --> 00:19:14,222
Treat this as slow jogging.

524
00:19:15,262 --> 00:19:16,262
Slowly.

525
00:19:16,432 --> 00:19:18,192
Gosh, it's cold.

526
00:19:19,932 --> 00:19:21,531
(He begins from the front gate of Gwanghwamun...)

527
00:19:21,532 --> 00:19:23,102
(toward Gyeongbokgung Station.)

528
00:19:25,402 --> 00:19:26,641
It's so cold.

529
00:19:26,642 --> 00:19:28,342
That's the same pace as the walker's.

530
00:19:29,372 --> 00:19:31,471
- You just look at it yourself! - Listen.

531
00:19:31,472 --> 00:19:33,582
- He's a fast walker. - What is this?

532
00:19:34,042 --> 00:19:36,452
- Look at that. - He's the master of fast walking.

533
00:19:36,712 --> 00:19:37,882
Remember what Sean said?

534
00:19:37,982 --> 00:19:39,011
- Run slowly. - I must run slowly...

535
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,051
- for the 1st 3km. - Okay.

536
00:19:40,052 --> 00:19:41,982
- To follow his advice? - I'm warming up.

537
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:43,882
Okay. You're right about that.

538
00:19:44,452 --> 00:19:46,392
My gosh, it's cold. It's freezing today.

539
00:19:46,992 --> 00:19:48,421
(Moorathoner will brave the cold.)

540
00:19:48,422 --> 00:19:49,932
- You got this! - You got this!

541
00:19:50,862 --> 00:19:53,061
- Runners... - You got this!

542
00:19:53,062 --> 00:19:54,801
- Are you runners? - Yes.

543
00:19:54,802 --> 00:19:55,802
How far did you run today?

544
00:19:55,803 --> 00:19:57,171
We're going to run 7km now.

545
00:19:57,172 --> 00:19:58,731
Only 7km? I'm going to run 8km.

546
00:19:58,732 --> 00:20:01,472
- Let's go! - Let's go!

547
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:03,111
(He's off to an energetic start...)

548
00:20:03,112 --> 00:20:04,912
(thanks to the energy of his fellow runners.)

549
00:20:05,312 --> 00:20:07,342
All right. Let's make the puppy's nose.

550
00:20:08,282 --> 00:20:10,652
- One, two, three, four. - People in the back are calling.

551
00:20:11,482 --> 00:20:13,022
They're reporting about a crazy man.

552
00:20:13,452 --> 00:20:16,222
One, two, three, four.

553
00:20:20,092 --> 00:20:23,162
He told me to run slowly.

554
00:20:23,692 --> 00:20:26,332
(Just like his teacher advised him...)

555
00:20:26,602 --> 00:20:27,731
It's doable so far.

556
00:20:27,732 --> 00:20:29,061
(Easily keeping his pace)

557
00:20:29,062 --> 00:20:30,202
I ran for five minutes.

558
00:20:31,232 --> 00:20:33,042
Not here. I must go a little farther.

559
00:20:33,702 --> 00:20:36,372
Then I can run a full circle there. That will give me a nose.

560
00:20:39,242 --> 00:20:40,412
(Grabbing)

561
00:20:40,512 --> 00:20:42,212
- Hello. I thought I knew him. - Wait.

562
00:20:43,382 --> 00:20:44,782
- Who is that? - No. Hold on. Look.

563
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,751
- It's Bong Tae Gyu! - What?

564
00:20:46,752 --> 00:20:48,151
- What? - That's Bong Tae Gyu.

565
00:20:48,152 --> 00:20:49,281
What's Bong Tae Gyu doing there?

566
00:20:49,282 --> 00:20:51,692
- He lives in Seongbuk-dong. - What?

567
00:20:53,522 --> 00:20:54,821
My gosh. Hello.

568
00:20:54,822 --> 00:20:56,122
- What? - I thought I knew him.

569
00:20:58,332 --> 00:21:00,001
- You treated him like a stranger. - My gosh.

570
00:21:00,002 --> 00:21:02,332
You ran past him and said, "I thought I knew him."

571
00:21:02,502 --> 00:21:03,531
- I... - I just found out.

572
00:21:03,532 --> 00:21:04,601
You didn't recognize him?

573
00:21:04,602 --> 00:21:06,342
- People often hit me like that. - But...

574
00:21:06,502 --> 00:21:08,271
- But... - I know what you mean.

575
00:21:08,272 --> 00:21:09,671
- You do, right? - I know what you mean.

576
00:21:09,672 --> 00:21:11,511
- You could've recognized him. - I didn't.

577
00:21:11,512 --> 00:21:13,241
He has such a distinctive face.

578
00:21:13,242 --> 00:21:14,511
He was self-absorbed then.

579
00:21:14,512 --> 00:21:16,712
- Right. I was. - He couldn't see anyone else. Yes.

580
00:21:17,252 --> 00:21:19,312
I feel so bad. I should text him today.

581
00:21:21,352 --> 00:21:23,752
(Immersed in running, he fails to recognize his friend.)

582
00:21:24,522 --> 00:21:25,622
All right.

583
00:21:26,262 --> 00:21:28,062
I drew the bottom of the nose.

584
00:21:30,762 --> 00:21:31,891
I guess he has to turn like that.

585
00:21:31,892 --> 00:21:34,332
I memorized that I must turn around the buckwheat restaurant.

586
00:21:34,602 --> 00:21:36,631
After starting at the jaw, I must turn a small corner.

587
00:21:36,632 --> 00:21:37,832
That's the nose part.

588
00:21:38,532 --> 00:21:40,902
I need the black nose to complete the puppy.

589
00:21:43,312 --> 00:21:45,241
- I see. You're turning like that. - That's... Yes.

590
00:21:45,242 --> 00:21:46,341
(For the round nose, he must run a block.)

591
00:21:46,342 --> 00:21:48,482
I had to run a block here.

592
00:21:48,842 --> 00:21:50,512
Passing the Korean restaurant...

593
00:21:53,352 --> 00:21:55,251
You must know the area to be able to run there.

594
00:21:55,252 --> 00:21:57,251
That's why I watched the video over ten times.

595
00:21:57,252 --> 00:21:58,291
- Really? - I see.

596
00:21:58,292 --> 00:21:59,721
You'd get the wrong shape if you get confused.

597
00:21:59,722 --> 00:22:01,162
- Right. - Right.

598
00:22:03,562 --> 00:22:05,631
All right. I just drew the nose.

599
00:22:05,632 --> 00:22:06,802
That's fascinating.

600
00:22:08,262 --> 00:22:09,602
I can do this.

601
00:22:10,032 --> 00:22:11,702
There are specific spots.

602
00:22:12,072 --> 00:22:13,641
Here are the parts I'm paying special attention to.

603
00:22:13,642 --> 00:22:15,542
The nose, the ear,

604
00:22:16,272 --> 00:22:17,572
- and the tail. - The tail.

605
00:22:17,842 --> 00:22:20,242
- If I mess up any of them, - Right.

606
00:22:20,342 --> 00:22:22,082
It would ruin the whole drawing.

607
00:22:22,242 --> 00:22:25,052
GPS running is similar to Moosquiat drawing art.

608
00:22:25,252 --> 00:22:27,782
That's the main part I'm focusing on.

609
00:22:28,922 --> 00:22:30,252
I already ran 1km.

610
00:22:30,692 --> 00:22:32,692
- You ran pretty far. - I finished 1km quite fast.

611
00:22:33,392 --> 00:22:35,222
Let's go and draw the head.

612
00:22:36,932 --> 00:22:38,792
(Jogging at ease)

613
00:22:41,602 --> 00:22:42,962
This part was difficult.

614
00:22:43,972 --> 00:22:45,202
This is it.

615
00:22:47,072 --> 00:22:49,271
The stonewall by Gyeongbokgung.

616
00:22:49,272 --> 00:22:51,072
(The stonewall path by Gyeongbokgung)

617
00:22:51,272 --> 00:22:52,441
Is it slightly hilly?

618
00:22:52,442 --> 00:22:53,942
It's not hilly. The path is plain.

619
00:22:54,282 --> 00:22:55,912
I just have to run along the wall.

620
00:22:56,652 --> 00:22:58,551
Seeing restaurants would boost your energy.

621
00:22:58,552 --> 00:22:59,952
I need to smell some food.

622
00:23:01,882 --> 00:23:05,351
(He draws the puppy head by running along the stonewall.)

623
00:23:05,352 --> 00:23:06,392
I knew it.

624
00:23:06,862 --> 00:23:08,322
It's getting hard right about now.

625
00:23:08,962 --> 00:23:09,962
(Panting)

626
00:23:10,532 --> 00:23:12,172
Why does this puppy have such a big head?

627
00:23:15,402 --> 00:23:18,672
(He must run around a bigger block for the head compared to the nose.)

628
00:23:20,772 --> 00:23:22,272
Honestly, I'm a bit surprised.

629
00:23:22,542 --> 00:23:24,372
I watched you run closely.

630
00:23:24,442 --> 00:23:27,112
Your posture is surprisingly better than I expected.

631
00:23:27,312 --> 00:23:29,751
- Really? - I see. Is his posture good?

632
00:23:29,752 --> 00:23:30,812
It's not bad.

633
00:23:30,852 --> 00:23:31,852
(My posture?)

634
00:23:31,852 --> 00:23:32,852
- Really? - Yes.

635
00:23:32,853 --> 00:23:34,351
When people aren't taught properly,

636
00:23:34,352 --> 00:23:36,522
their heels touch first while running.

637
00:23:36,852 --> 00:23:38,351
But your midfoot touches the ground first.

638
00:23:38,352 --> 00:23:39,551
(Hyun Moo can already land on his midfoot first.)

639
00:23:39,552 --> 00:23:41,961
Usually, their upper body shake like this.

640
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:44,191
- But your upper body is fixed. - You're right.

641
00:23:44,192 --> 00:23:47,032
It's harder to fix your upper body while running.

642
00:23:47,332 --> 00:23:48,901
Your posture is quite good.

643
00:23:48,902 --> 00:23:50,331
- It's good? - I was surprised.

644
00:23:50,332 --> 00:23:51,402
I was born to be a runner.

645
00:23:54,872 --> 00:23:55,972
Hello.

646
00:23:56,372 --> 00:23:57,911
So many people are running there.

647
00:23:57,912 --> 00:23:59,012
My fellow runners.

648
00:23:59,612 --> 00:24:01,882
Runners just get each other. You know?

649
00:24:02,742 --> 00:24:04,882
You only get this feeling after a good sweat.

650
00:24:06,582 --> 00:24:08,151
Don't talk. Just run.

651
00:24:08,152 --> 00:24:09,822
(You must be tired.)

652
00:24:11,422 --> 00:24:12,582
My gosh, it's the Blue House.

653
00:24:13,792 --> 00:24:16,391
I'm running around the Blue House and around the wall...

654
00:24:16,392 --> 00:24:17,532
by Gyeongbokgung Palace.

655
00:24:17,892 --> 00:24:19,231
I went around the Blue House.

656
00:24:19,232 --> 00:24:20,931
(As he goes around the Blue House, )

657
00:24:20,932 --> 00:24:22,732
(he makes out the top of the head.)

658
00:24:30,342 --> 00:24:31,982
I'm seeing everything I saw in the video.

659
00:24:34,142 --> 00:24:36,911
(He runs and runs as he studied in advance.)

660
00:24:36,912 --> 00:24:39,382
Yes, I know this neighborhood. It's Samcheong-dong.

661
00:24:39,682 --> 00:24:40,751
Samcheong-dong.

662
00:24:40,752 --> 00:24:41,921
- It's a nice neighborhood. - Samcheong-dong is nice.

663
00:24:41,922 --> 00:24:43,421
(It's where he'll draw the ear of the puppy.)

664
00:24:43,422 --> 00:24:44,491
The ear is important.

665
00:24:44,492 --> 00:24:46,822
(It's where he'll draw the ear of the puppy.)

666
00:24:49,492 --> 00:24:50,532
Sujebi.

667
00:24:51,792 --> 00:24:53,501
- It's famous. - That restaurant is delicious.

668
00:24:53,502 --> 00:24:55,562
(That restaurant is delicious!)

669
00:24:55,932 --> 00:24:57,372
There isn't a line today.

670
00:24:59,072 --> 00:25:01,171
(Sniffing)

671
00:25:01,172 --> 00:25:02,341
I could smell it.

672
00:25:02,342 --> 00:25:03,611
(He keeps running as he smells the air.)

673
00:25:03,612 --> 00:25:04,892
Will you pass by the restaurant?

674
00:25:07,212 --> 00:25:08,692
Where am I? Am I going the right way?

675
00:25:11,712 --> 00:25:12,852
What?

676
00:25:15,022 --> 00:25:16,022
I'm lost.

677
00:25:16,023 --> 00:25:17,622
- He's lost. - Oh, no.

678
00:25:17,892 --> 00:25:19,492
The ear needs to come out nicely.

679
00:25:20,922 --> 00:25:22,692
(Worried)

680
00:25:23,162 --> 00:25:24,592
Where am I?

681
00:25:26,862 --> 00:25:28,402
I don't want to stop.

682
00:25:30,102 --> 00:25:32,201
(He checks the map as he walks.)

683
00:25:32,202 --> 00:25:33,941
After passing Churro 101,

684
00:25:33,942 --> 00:25:36,171
I need to cross the road in front of KFCC.

685
00:25:36,172 --> 00:25:37,688
(The turning point for the puppy ear is a bank.)

686
00:25:37,712 --> 00:25:39,011
I need to find KFCC.

687
00:25:39,012 --> 00:25:40,682
(He needs to find a bank.)

688
00:25:41,682 --> 00:25:42,781
KFCC.

689
00:25:42,782 --> 00:25:44,281
(He keeps going straight in search of a turning point.)

690
00:25:44,282 --> 00:25:45,552
Where's KFCC?

691
00:25:47,922 --> 00:25:48,922
- Oh, no. - I was going insane...

692
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:49,922
because I couldn't see it.

693
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:51,563
(Moorathoner's expression turns serious.)

694
00:25:51,952 --> 00:25:53,022
Hello.

695
00:25:53,152 --> 00:25:54,692
Sir, do you know where KFCC is?

696
00:25:55,722 --> 00:25:57,762
- KFCC? - Yes. Did I pass it?

697
00:25:57,992 --> 00:25:59,391
- Oh, no. - Did I pass it?

698
00:25:59,392 --> 00:26:01,662
- It's over there. - You should go there again.

699
00:26:03,732 --> 00:26:06,131
- Do you see that over there? - Yes.

700
00:26:06,132 --> 00:26:08,772
If you travel that distance once more, it'll be on your right.

701
00:26:09,472 --> 00:26:10,512
Thank you.

702
00:26:12,012 --> 00:26:14,442
The ear... I ruined it. For goodness' sake.

703
00:26:15,112 --> 00:26:16,182
How annoying!

704
00:26:16,782 --> 00:26:18,982
(Wellness!)

705
00:26:19,382 --> 00:26:21,552
I got distracted by that sujebi place...

706
00:26:21,882 --> 00:26:23,152
and missed KFCC.

707
00:26:23,692 --> 00:26:25,021
For goodness' sake. That sujebi place.

708
00:26:25,022 --> 00:26:26,321
(The sujebi place that distracted Moorathoner is back.)

709
00:26:26,322 --> 00:26:28,392
- That restaurant is tasty. - It's tasty.

710
00:26:29,422 --> 00:26:31,062
KFCC was here.

711
00:26:31,892 --> 00:26:34,231
It was right next to the sujebi place.

712
00:26:34,232 --> 00:26:35,778
I missed it because of the sujebi place.

713
00:26:35,802 --> 00:26:37,601
I should've turned around here. For goodness' sake.

714
00:26:37,602 --> 00:26:39,001
(I missed it because of the sujebi place.)

715
00:26:39,002 --> 00:26:40,072
I'm so upset.

716
00:26:42,472 --> 00:26:44,071
Just how much more did I run?

717
00:26:44,072 --> 00:26:46,071
(Just how much more did I run?)

718
00:26:46,072 --> 00:26:47,482
- The ear. - It became long.

719
00:26:47,942 --> 00:26:50,181
- No. Let's say it's a dobermann. - That's right.

720
00:26:50,182 --> 00:26:51,681
- Let's say it's a dobermann. - That's right.

721
00:26:51,682 --> 00:26:53,752
- It became a rabbit. - It looks cute.

722
00:26:54,222 --> 00:26:55,952
I practically made a deer antler.

723
00:26:56,552 --> 00:26:58,291
I got distracted by sujebi.

724
00:26:58,292 --> 00:27:01,022
I never had that sujebi without waiting in a line.

725
00:27:01,662 --> 00:27:03,732
But there was no line. It got me excited.

726
00:27:04,062 --> 00:27:05,632
"Should I have a bowl?"

727
00:27:05,932 --> 00:27:07,632
"It'd be a win since there's no line."

728
00:27:07,932 --> 00:27:09,632
I got distracted then.

729
00:27:10,202 --> 00:27:12,702
I should've turned there to make a pretty ear,

730
00:27:13,002 --> 00:27:15,572
- but I kept going. - He made a lightning rod.

731
00:27:15,672 --> 00:27:17,442
I went up about 1km.

732
00:27:17,842 --> 00:27:19,241
I was so annoyed.

733
00:27:19,242 --> 00:27:21,442
I felt so victimized. I had wasted my energy.

734
00:27:23,452 --> 00:27:26,182
It was emotionally difficult.

735
00:27:26,982 --> 00:27:28,181
I lost a lot of my spirit then.

736
00:27:28,182 --> 00:27:29,182
(Oh, no)

737
00:27:29,183 --> 00:27:31,492
- Right. - I'm so upset.

738
00:27:35,862 --> 00:27:38,492
- How many kilometers have you run? - I'm so upset.

739
00:27:39,092 --> 00:27:41,362
About 3km, I think.

740
00:27:42,132 --> 00:27:44,331
That means you surpassed your personal record.

741
00:27:44,332 --> 00:27:45,371
- That's right. - That's right.

742
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,571
I surpassed my personal record.

743
00:27:46,572 --> 00:27:49,071
(Moorathoner makes a personal record of 3km)

744
00:27:49,072 --> 00:27:50,642
What's... Is that right?

745
00:27:51,742 --> 00:27:53,442
- Hello. - Hello.

746
00:27:54,082 --> 00:27:55,411
- I'm a fan! - Okay.

747
00:27:55,412 --> 00:27:57,511
- I ran all the way here. - I mean...

748
00:27:57,512 --> 00:27:58,951
- Take this. - Where is it from?

749
00:27:58,952 --> 00:28:01,051
- I'm checking out Seoul. Okay. - It's from my bakery.

750
00:28:01,052 --> 00:28:02,322
- Thank you. - Thank you.

751
00:28:03,992 --> 00:28:05,452
Is it okay to eat as I run?

752
00:28:05,722 --> 00:28:07,561
- Is it a toast? - It's pulppang.

753
00:28:07,562 --> 00:28:09,268
- It looks delicious. - It's pulppang that contains...

754
00:28:09,292 --> 00:28:11,031
- the high-quality red bean filling. - It looks delicious.

755
00:28:11,032 --> 00:28:12,062
(Humming in approval)

756
00:28:14,232 --> 00:28:15,232
It's good.

757
00:28:16,362 --> 00:28:20,041
Even marathoners eat simple snacks as they run.

758
00:28:20,042 --> 00:28:21,872
- Exactly. - It's so tasty.

759
00:28:22,402 --> 00:28:25,112
Hold on. Hyun Moo, hold on. Why...

760
00:28:25,272 --> 00:28:26,782
Sean said that I could walk.

761
00:28:27,012 --> 00:28:29,782
After warming up for 3km...

762
00:28:29,842 --> 00:28:32,811
and running for 5km, you can stop if you're exhausted.

763
00:28:32,812 --> 00:28:33,952
I was exhausted.

764
00:28:34,452 --> 00:28:35,881
- You got exhausted early on. - Yes.

765
00:28:35,882 --> 00:28:37,991
- It can't be helped. - You renewed a personal record.

766
00:28:37,992 --> 00:28:39,352
I renewed a personal record.

767
00:28:40,362 --> 00:28:41,791
(As he walks, he celebrates renewing a personal record.)

768
00:28:41,792 --> 00:28:43,292
He looks so weird.

769
00:28:44,632 --> 00:28:45,732
